<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104009/timeless-plate-armor-cache">
<img alt="Timeless Plate Armor Cache" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_19.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Timeless Plate Armor Cache</span></a></td>
<td>7500 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=777/timeless-coin">
<span>
<img alt="Timeless Coin" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/timelesscoin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Timeless Coin</span></span></a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Protection Paladins</span></h2>There are six Legendary cloaks available with four unique proc effects; for Protection Paladins, the choice is between the following two versions:<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table border="1" cellpadding="5" class="exclude-units markup-table-clean-borders" style="background:#222222;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center; width: 25%; max-width: 100%;">
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a></td>
<td style="text-align: center; width: 25%; max-width: 100%;">
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102249/gong-lu-strength-of-xuen">
<img alt="Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen</span></a></td></tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: center;">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146193/endurance-of-niuzao">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/monk_stance_drunkenox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Endurance of Niuzao</span></a>: The Endurance of Niuzao fully absorbs the damage of one attack that would normally kill you. This effect has a 2 min cooldown. Does not function for non-Tank-specialized characters.</td>
<td style="text-align: center;">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146195/flurry-of-xuen">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/monk_stance_whitetiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry of Xuen</span></a>: Your damaging attacks have a chance to trigger a Flurry of Xuen, causing you to deal 1 (+ 20% of Attack power) damage to up to 5 enemies in front of you, every 0.3 sec for 3 sec. (Approximately [1.74 + Haste] procs per minute).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>As for which cloak to wear, as is the case with pretty much every other offensive vs. defensive gearing decision in the game, it ultimately comes down to how confident you are in the abilities of you and your raid. The cheat-death effect of <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a>  of is special in that the effect is entirely passive, meaning that it will always work, even in the most dire and chaotic of circumstances. It excels for progression content, and quite frankly, unless there is a major dps-check in the way of your success and you specifically rely on tank damage, just getting more tries further into the encounter is likely to shorten your progression considerably. <br/>
<br/>That being said, the offensive benefit of  <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102249/gong-lu-strength-of-xuen">
<img alt="Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen</span></a> is non-negligible, as the stats are ideal and the proc scales with Vengeance. Overall, you can expect the cloak to increase your damage by 5% on single-target fights.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Protection Paladin Trinkets</span></h2>Siege of Orgrimmar features many interesting and potent trinket options, often fitting very particular niches. Since none of the trinkets affect our Hit or Expertise caps, this makes it easy to swap around trinkets on demand, a clear and welcome deviation from our struggles during earlier tiers.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105609/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> - An excellent trinket, supplementing both our offensive and defensive capabilities. A must-have for every set, but the same applies for all other classes, so be ready for some competition. Note that wearing the Caster and Agility options is possible, but not good enough to make the cut for this list.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> - This is the second trinket making it into the default offensive lineup. It is ever so slightly stronger than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105527/haromms-talisman">
<img alt="Haromm's Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haromm's Talisman</span></a>, performing roughly 0.30% better on patchwerk fights, but suffering when proc uptime and damage phases desynchronize.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105527/haromms-talisman">
<img alt="Haromm's Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haromm's Talisman</span></a> &amp; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105540/kardris-toxic-totem">
<img alt="Kardris' Toxic Totem" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Kardris' Toxic Totem</span></a>   -  Shared third position, dipping into Caster and Agility-class territory simply to gain access to multistrike, performing better than the aforementioned <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> for fights with uneven uptime. Between those three offensive trinkets for your second slot, simply pick whichever option is less contested.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105459/fusion-fire-core">
<img alt="Fusion-Fire Core" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion-Fire Core</span></a> - Simply swap into this trinket for fights where cleave damage is useful.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105568/vial-of-living-corruption">
<img alt="Vial of Living Corruption" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Living Corruption</span></a> - This trinket reduces the cooldowns of all of our major defensive abilities, on a class which relies on chaining their defensive abilities. Clear first pick by a decent margin. The worst part of this trinket is how hard it is to take off, since you will have to relearn encounter timings.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105645/curse-of-hubris">
<img alt="Curse of Hubris" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Curse of Hubris</span></a> - Surprisingly decent, arguably balanced, option, especially in fights where you can expect to achieve maximum Vengeance during a burst-phase.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105438/rooks-unlucky-talisman">
<img alt="Rook's Unlucky Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rook's Unlucky Talisman</span></a> - Interesting option with very niche utility. Almost all of the AOE options in the current tier are dodgeable, relegating this trinket to potential-cheese status.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102706/prideful-gladiators-emblem-of-tenacity">
<img alt="Prideful Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_endlessrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Prideful Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity</span></a> - As in previous tiers, the usefulness of an on-demand HP boost on a generally worthwhile stamina statbase should not be underestimated. However, in the final tier the scaling simply doesn't stay up to par to make this Trinket anything but a progression pick on new characters, because of how easy it is to acquire.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Protection Paladins</span></h2>Crafted gear is no longer profession locked for the most part, meaning even non-Blacksmiths can use Blacksmithing items. The main exceptions are <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a>  and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a>, which still require their respective profession skills to be equipped. Crafted gear at 476 item level is ideal for pre-MSV gearing or as an affordable option afterwards, while the 496 versions will hold Pre-BiS status until you start raiding on Normal or Heroic difficulty.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98607/avengers-trillium-legplates">
<img alt="Avenger's Trillium Legplates" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_40v3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Avenger's Trillium Legplates</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98616/avengers-trillium-waistplate">
<img alt="Avenger's Trillium Waistplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_93v3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Avenger's Trillium Waistplate</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98606/protectors-trillium-legguards">
<img alt="Protector's Trillium Legguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_40.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Protector's Trillium Legguards</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98615/protectors-trillium-waistguard">
<img alt="Protector's Trillium Waistguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Protector's Trillium Waistguard</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94265/haunted-steel-treads">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Treads</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94266/haunted-steel-greathelm">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Greathelm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Greathelm</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94267/haunted-steel-warboots">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Warboots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Warboots</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94268/haunted-steel-headguard">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Headguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Headguard</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Paladins</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit, whereas for Expertise the caps are split into 7.5% Expertise to reach the so-called "soft cap" and 15% Expertise to reach the true "hard cap." Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei racial Heroic Presence, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your melee hits no longer miss raid bosses. Spells, however, operate on a different Hit table and it would require additional investment into Hit to negate this miss chance entirely. In Mists of Pandaria, there exists another option: most Tanks will now look to solve their Spell Hit woes through Expertise.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attack, but they can still parry them. For most raid encounters, you should aim to reach the full 15% Expertise cap to eliminate both dodge and parry from the equation. All gear sets recommended in this guide will meet this cap. There are exceptions, though—some raid bosses cannot parry, due to encounter mechanics or positioning. In those cases, it may be wise to reforge or swap gear to favor other stats.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, reaching 7.5% Expertise will also make you achieve Spell Hit cap, ensuring your spells such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=26573/consecration">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_innerfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Consecration</span></a> won't miss.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Protection Paladins</span></h2>Given the amount of stat inflation, even Pre-BIS gear sets will usually be able to gem for haste instead of option for Expertise or Hit gems. Still, It's usually worth aiming for socket bonuses that grant Expertise, Hit, Haste, or Stamina in roughly that order of priority. To meet those bonuses efficiently, make use of hybrid gems, like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76667/wicked-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Wicked Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wicked Vermilion Onyx</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76681/accurate-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Accurate Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Accurate Imperial Amethyst</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76642/lightning-wild-jade">
<img alt="Lightning Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning Wild Jade</span></a>. On certain fights with highly unpredictable spike damage, you may want to consider swapping in more <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76639/solid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Solid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid River's Heart</span></a>  or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a>, if your caps allow. <br/>
<br/>Finally, keep in mind that <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76895/austere-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Austere Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Austere Primal Diamond</span></a> will always stick around as a meta gem option to increase your survivability, although <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a> will likely be the most common pick once you've geared up a bit. Once you've progressed your legendary quest line, the new legendary meta gems will become available and should be used, with <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> being the default choice.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
